WEBVTT

00:01.380 --> 00:04.160
All your sins are trivial.

00:04.160 --> 00:10.320
Now, then. There is an answer as to how 
President Otonashi killed Sumi-san.

00:11.730 --> 00:13.260
Please think carefully.

01:23.410 --> 01:25.490
I'm going to get some fresh air.

01:26.550 --> 01:30.120
I should at least let Kaoruko 
know what's going on.

01:32.360 --> 01:35.290
I'm going to get some air, too.

02:06.020 --> 02:07.720
Feeling a little tired?

02:08.030 --> 02:10.060
Shall we head back to our room, as well?

02:10.060 --> 02:11.410
No, thanks.

02:11.410 --> 02:14.370
There's no telling what you'd 
do to me when we got there.

02:14.370 --> 02:16.190
We'll be together tonight anyway, right?

02:16.790 --> 02:19.990
Kuro-senpai, you look good in a suit.

02:20.210 --> 02:22.430
Why not use one for pajamas?

02:22.430 --> 02:23.990
It'd be too hard to sleep in.

02:24.930 --> 02:30.580
Is President Otonashi aware that everyone 
at the time had their own murder plan?

02:30.800 --> 02:34.540
No, I used my own theories and 
the information I'd gathered

02:34.540 --> 02:36.760
to bait them into telling me.

02:37.030 --> 02:40.350
The president has no way of knowing.

02:40.350 --> 02:43.600
Then was there any need to bring it up?

02:43.830 --> 02:47.250
If President Otonashi finds out, 
he'll be very surprised.

02:47.250 --> 02:50.730
Give people a strange task, 
and strange things will happen.

02:51.330 --> 02:54.900
I'll tell him sometime today, I suppose.

02:55.240 --> 02:57.270
Also, like I said, if I hadn't brought it up,

02:57.270 --> 03:01.190
they might have thought about things 
I didn't want them thinking about.

03:01.190 --> 03:02.390
Doing that made it easier

03:02.390 --> 03:06.790
to lead them to the appropriate false 
solution that I've prepared for them.

03:07.030 --> 03:11.200
You're not going to wait for them to 
come up with that solution on their own?

03:11.200 --> 03:13.040
It's easier if I don't.

03:13.260 --> 03:17.490
I've left a decent number of clues to help 
them come to the solution I've prepared.

03:17.490 --> 03:20.430
Give them time to think more about 
what kind of person the victim was

03:20.430 --> 03:21.930
and what was going on at the time,

03:22.300 --> 03:25.170
and perhaps they'll come to the 
conclusion with no more help from me.

03:25.510 --> 03:28.560
Rion-san's the most likely 
to do so, as I see it.

03:28.890 --> 03:33.590
She may reach the conclusion 
I want as soon as tonight.

03:34.580 --> 03:38.120
<i>I was prepared for my and 
Susumu's sin to come to light.</i>

03:38.120 --> 03:40.070
<i>But I didn't expect that 
it wouldn't end there.</i>

03:40.300 --> 03:43.110
Though I was shocked to learn what 
Kaoruko and Koya-san were up to...

03:43.110 --> 03:46.700
If you thought this was going to happen, 
you should've come yourself, Dad.

03:46.700 --> 03:48.140
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

03:49.010 --> 03:51.050
I didn't know what to do.

03:51.050 --> 03:54.120
I thought I would need to hide that 
part of my past until the day I died,

03:54.380 --> 03:58.280
but I also thought it might 
be easier if you and Dad knew.

03:58.280 --> 04:00.610
So I was fine with the idea of you

04:00.610 --> 04:03.380
finding out on your own,
or Dad denouncing me for it.

04:03.620 --> 04:06.260
I just didn't want to say anything on my own.

04:06.260 --> 04:07.940
Oh, yeah.

04:07.940 --> 04:13.490
Uncle Susumu was practically forced to 
confess by Iwanaga Kotoko, so I get it.

04:13.490 --> 04:14.850
I won't get mad at you.

04:15.140 --> 04:18.010
Considering your father tried 
to murder your grandmother,

04:18.010 --> 04:19.150
you don't seem very angry.

04:19.150 --> 04:20.420
<i>you don't seem very angry.</i>

04:21.740 --> 04:27.060
I just can't figure out what 
kind of person Grandmother was.

04:27.060 --> 04:29.660
So it just doesn't seem real...

04:30.180 --> 04:34.160
People tell me she's the one who grew 
the Otonashi Group to its current size.

04:34.430 --> 04:39.550
but also that she was so problematic 
that her own family plotted to kill her.

04:40.190 --> 04:45.310
But you and Uncle Susumu, 
and even Uncle Koya and Grandpa...

04:45.310 --> 04:48.800
When all of you talk about her, 
it doesn't feel like you hate her.

04:48.800 --> 04:53.060
There's no real anger there, 
even though you all wanted to kill her.

04:53.060 --> 04:56.350
That's why it just doesn't feel real.

04:56.350 --> 05:00.270
Yeah... Back then, I did hate her.

05:00.730 --> 05:03.690
If she's alive, it will ruin everything!

05:04.950 --> 05:06.700
That's what everybody said.

05:06.700 --> 05:10.850
But she's been gone a long time, and 
in that time, I've come to understand...

05:11.320 --> 05:14.440
She wasn't a tyrant who never 
listened to the people around her,

05:14.440 --> 05:17.580
and it wasn't that she didn't 
care about our happiness.

05:17.580 --> 05:20.130
She was a victim, too.

05:20.130 --> 05:22.590
She just believed the orders she was given,

05:22.590 --> 05:25.470
<i>and carried them out. Nothing more.</i>

05:25.470 --> 05:27.090
Orders?

05:27.090 --> 05:28.290
<i>From who?</i>

05:28.290 --> 05:31.510
Her father, Denjiro.

05:33.420 --> 05:36.340
My mother was the one who 
made the Otonashi Group huge,

05:36.340 --> 05:39.230
but it was Denjiro who told her to do it.

05:39.510 --> 05:42.650
He put together detailed 
plans for growing the group,

05:42.650 --> 05:44.530
<i>and he entrusted them to her.</i>

05:44.910 --> 05:49.180
Otonashi Sumi did nothing but carry 
out the orders she was given.

05:49.870 --> 05:51.960
Her marriage to your grandfather, Goichi,

05:51.960 --> 05:55.220
was something Denjiro 
decided without asking her.

05:55.570 --> 06:01.080
Denjiro decided how many children the group 
needed, how they would inherit the group,

06:01.080 --> 06:07.380
and who they would marry. 
And she obeyed his every word.

06:07.380 --> 06:11.110
Denjiro's instructions were that specific.

06:11.570 --> 06:15.470
That's why, as the eldest son, 
I was ordered to take over the group,

06:15.470 --> 06:18.350
and Susumu was never to be more than my aide.

06:18.350 --> 06:22.330
And she tried to make Kaoruko 
break up with Koya-san so that

06:22.330 --> 06:24.570
she could marry someone from a good family.

06:24.570 --> 06:28.610
To her, that was the way for 
all of us to be happiest,

06:28.610 --> 06:30.790
and what would benefit the 
group the most, as well.

06:32.680 --> 06:34.200
<i>And what's really scary is this:</i>

06:34.510 --> 06:38.330
while she was alive, it all worked.

06:39.130 --> 06:41.800
The group was expanding steadily,

06:41.800 --> 06:45.000
along the lines Denjiro had 
laid out during his life.

06:45.240 --> 06:47.620
The husband he'd chosen for her was

06:47.620 --> 06:50.380
a talented man who did his 
job of supporting her perfectly.

06:50.380 --> 06:55.310
Susumu, Kaoruko, and I all grew up 
into the children she wanted us to be.

06:55.310 --> 06:58.410
She did everything Denjiro wanted, 
eliminated anyone who got in her way,

06:58.410 --> 07:01.060
and continued to succeed 
for over half a century.

07:01.060 --> 07:04.820
Is someone like that capable of 
suddenly not following orders?

07:05.210 --> 07:08.750
Could she decide an order 
was wrong, and disobey it?

07:09.480 --> 07:14.160
Especially when nothing she'd 
done so far had clearly failed?

07:16.130 --> 07:19.690
<i>It would take an incredible 
amount of courage.</i>

07:19.690 --> 07:23.220
<i>It might mean denying everything 
you'd done in your entire life.</i>

07:23.220 --> 07:23.920
Yes.

07:24.210 --> 07:27.300
<i>She was Denjiro's puppet.</i>

07:27.300 --> 07:30.610
<i>I think the truth is that she 
knew the group was in danger,</i>

07:30.610 --> 07:34.300
<i>and that her children wanted to 
find happiness in different ways.</i>

07:34.600 --> 07:39.410
<i>But admitting that and changing her 
policies would mean disobeying Denjiro,</i>

07:39.410 --> 07:42.120
<i>and abandoning something that 
had succeeded her entire life.</i>

07:42.510 --> 07:45.790
But she couldn't do that, because it worked.

07:45.790 --> 07:51.070
<i>Yeah. That's why she...  
why Mom died at the best time.</i>

07:51.420 --> 07:55.420
Because she died then, she never 
had to see the group collapsing,

07:55.420 --> 07:58.200
or her children becoming 
miserable due to her actions.

07:58.200 --> 08:04.210
She was able to avoid seeing what 
she'd believed in betray her completely.

08:04.210 --> 08:06.570
She was lucky, as I see it.

08:07.970 --> 08:12.470
But I don't think that means 
I was right to try to kill her.

08:12.780 --> 08:15.720
I was just doing it for my own future.

08:16.020 --> 08:19.370
But you couldn't carry out 
your plan on your own, right?

08:19.370 --> 08:22.230
So you went to Uncle Susumu...

08:22.230 --> 08:26.230
Once I get focused on something, 
I lose sight of everything else.

08:26.540 --> 08:29.690
Susumu's much calmer. 
He can see the big picture.

08:29.690 --> 08:32.190
I trusted his vision more than anything.

08:32.430 --> 08:35.030
I'm not cut out to lead the group.

08:35.030 --> 08:39.340
<i>If I'd taken it over, 
it would've been a disaster.</i>

08:39.340 --> 08:42.670
<i>You should tell him that!</i>

08:42.670 --> 08:46.370
I have, many times! 
But he refuses to believe me.

08:46.370 --> 08:47.540
<i>That might've been why</i>

08:47.870 --> 08:52.130
you were able to refuse to follow 
the orders you were given.

08:52.410 --> 08:56.540
You weren't satisfied being in the 
places Grandmother prepared for you,

08:56.540 --> 08:59.760
so your desire to find your own path won out.

08:59.760 --> 09:00.970
<i>That's right.</i>

09:00.970 --> 09:04.660
<i>If we'd followed her orders 
and experienced success,</i>

09:04.660 --> 09:08.920
<i>we might've become Denjiro's puppets, too.</i>

09:09.690 --> 09:13.830
Success sometimes harms people and 
leads them to their own destruction.

09:14.340 --> 09:18.070
<i>Was she giving me hints the whole time?</i>

09:18.590 --> 09:21.480
<i>Everyone had an alibi and a murder plan.</i>

09:21.480 --> 09:24.710
<i>A planned murder wouldn't have given 
the victim a chance to scream.</i>

09:25.000 --> 09:30.210
<i>Every person's story had contradictions. 
Something that removed them from suspicion.</i>

09:31.130 --> 09:32.960
<i>But with this theory...</i>

09:33.450 --> 09:38.430
Dad, you said Grandmother 
died at a good time, right?

09:38.430 --> 09:40.550
I did. But why?

09:40.770 --> 09:44.560
I think I might have figured this out.

09:56.280 --> 10:01.150
I think I figured out the truth 
behind the murder 23 years ago.

10:01.830 --> 10:04.790
<i>I didn't feel any excitement 
at finding the answer.</i>

10:05.640 --> 10:10.410
<i>Iwanaga Kotoko had laid it out 
for me to find from the start.</i>

10:16.320 --> 10:21.010
<b>Uninvited Judge</b>

10:21.420 --> 10:23.640
Grandmother committed suicide.

10:23.640 --> 10:27.020
That's why everyone, 
including my grandfather, had an alibi.

10:29.700 --> 10:34.260
Rion, your grandmother 
would never commit suicide.

10:34.260 --> 10:39.230
She ruled the people around her with an 
iron fist. She had no reason to kill herself.

10:39.230 --> 10:42.320
But it was clear the group was 
going to fall apart, right?

10:42.320 --> 10:46.580
That's why you were all plotting to kill her.

10:46.580 --> 10:49.880
And Uncle Susumu and Uncle Koya,

10:49.880 --> 10:52.600
you both realized that Grandmother's 
success had trapped her,

10:52.600 --> 10:56.130
and there was no way for her 
to stop what she was doing.

10:56.130 --> 11:00.880
We're older now. We see things 
differently than we did then.

11:00.880 --> 11:05.520
So we don't hate her. 
We know our mother was a victim, too.

11:05.520 --> 11:08.730
She had ample reason to kill herself.

11:09.040 --> 11:11.410
She was an excellent businesswoman,

11:11.410 --> 11:13.980
smart enough to know that if she 
kept following Denjiro's orders,

11:14.410 --> 11:17.130
the group would go bankrupt.

11:17.750 --> 11:21.460
The group's collapse would be tantamount 
to disobeying Denjiro's orders.

11:21.460 --> 11:23.640
She had to avoid that at all costs.

11:23.870 --> 11:27.860
But not doing what he told her 
to would be a betrayal, too.

11:28.870 --> 11:32.540
To her, that must've been terrifying.

11:32.940 --> 11:36.170
Given how much success she'd experienced 
by doing what she'd been told,

11:36.170 --> 11:37.980
that was impossible.

11:38.440 --> 11:42.800
The only way out of it was suicide.

11:43.140 --> 11:47.190
It was the only way she could protect 
the Otonashi Group and escape from

11:47.190 --> 11:48.890
the terror she was feeling.

11:50.980 --> 11:54.750
But... Mom? Committing suicide?

11:55.140 --> 12:00.520
I'll grant that back then, I thought 
everything would be resolved if she died.

12:00.520 --> 12:02.490
And I was right!

12:02.840 --> 12:07.370
If Mom knew that, then perhaps 
she might choose to end her life.

12:07.370 --> 12:13.100
But wouldn't it have been easier to disobey 
Denjiro's orders than kill herself?

12:13.100 --> 12:16.710
When you're under that much pressure, 
it's common to take the easy way out.

12:16.710 --> 12:19.430
Whenever that happens, 
the people around you will say,

12:19.430 --> 12:21.400
"You should've just quit your job,"

12:21.400 --> 12:24.720
or "You should've just cut them out 
of your life," as if it's that easy.

12:25.130 --> 12:26.490
But from the victim's perspective,

12:26.490 --> 12:28.100
<b>Stress</b>

12:26.490 --> 12:30.100
they have responsibilities, or they're 
too scared of what come after.

12:28.100 --> 12:29.350
<b>Stress</b>

12:28.120 --> 12:29.350
<b>Pressure</b>

12:29.350 --> 12:30.350
<b>Stress</b>

12:29.350 --> 12:30.350
<b>Pressure</b>

12:29.370 --> 12:30.350
<b>Work</b>

12:30.100 --> 12:31.600
That's why suicide is so appealing.

12:30.350 --> 12:31.600
<b>Stress</b>

12:30.350 --> 12:31.600
<b>Pressure</b>

12:30.350 --> 12:31.600
<b>Work</b>

12:30.370 --> 12:31.600
<b>Relationships</b>

12:31.870 --> 12:35.530
It offers an escape from responsibilities, 
and you don't need to know what happens after.

12:37.130 --> 12:39.570
If you have someone you can share 
your responsibilities with

12:39.570 --> 12:41.740
and talk to about what 
to do next, it's different.

12:42.160 --> 12:44.910
But Sumi-san didn't have 
anyone like that, right?

12:46.100 --> 12:50.290
At that point, death was a blessing for her.

12:50.290 --> 12:56.210
My father said the same thing. 
She died at the best time. She was lucky.

12:56.970 --> 13:00.210
That means choosing death was 
a compelling alternative for her.

13:00.520 --> 13:03.540
But a simple suicide wasn't an option.

13:03.540 --> 13:07.890
The death of a leader of a group 
that size would bring shame to it.

13:07.890 --> 13:09.710
It would damage the brand's image.

13:10.090 --> 13:14.260
She'd be doing it to protect the group. 
So that wasn't an option for her.

13:14.750 --> 13:18.470
Thus, she needed to die in a way 
that made people suspicious.

13:18.860 --> 13:22.360
So it was a suicide made to look like a murder?

13:22.640 --> 13:24.610
Made to look like a robbery gone wrong?

13:24.610 --> 13:26.740
<b>Okamoto
Osteopathic Clinic</b>

13:25.100 --> 13:28.080
She was alone on her way back 
from the massage parlor,

13:28.080 --> 13:31.740
and walking through an 
empty residential area.

13:32.240 --> 13:35.770
That's where she put her plan into action.

13:37.500 --> 13:39.210
To make it look like the robber

13:39.210 --> 13:42.720
stole her bag and took the bills 
from her wallet before running,

13:42.720 --> 13:44.740
she made sure she wasn't carrying any money,

13:44.740 --> 13:47.010
and threw the wallet and bag on the ground.

13:47.470 --> 13:49.780
Then she took out the knife 
she was secretly carrying.

13:50.220 --> 13:53.600
But wasn't the knife devoid of fingerprints?

13:53.900 --> 14:00.480
She used the hem of her jacket to keep 
her fingers from touching the knife grip.

14:00.480 --> 14:06.240
And then, to make it clear that 
it was a murder, she screamed.

14:10.160 --> 14:11.420
Thief!

14:11.420 --> 14:15.040
Somebody, get the man in the black jacket!

14:15.270 --> 14:16.690
He ran toward the station!

14:16.690 --> 14:20.540
Now no one would suspect suicide.

14:20.540 --> 14:23.870
That accomplished most of her goal,

14:23.870 --> 14:27.420
but a murder would surely be 
investigated by the police.

14:30.930 --> 14:34.250
If suspicion were to fall upon 
 the members of the group,

14:34.250 --> 14:36.790
it would damage the brand's image.

14:37.130 --> 14:40.770
Thus, she killed herself at a 
time when everyone had an alibi,

14:41.240 --> 14:44.190
and thus no one would be under suspicion.

14:45.030 --> 14:47.570
It makes sense.

14:47.570 --> 14:53.250
But if Mom killed herself, 
then why did Dad say he did it?

14:53.250 --> 14:58.910
Is it possible that Grandfather carefully 
manipulated her into killing herself?

14:59.190 --> 15:03.290
Made her believe that 
it was the best way out,

15:03.290 --> 15:12.690
and then gave her the information that he 
was sure would be the last push she needed?

15:16.050 --> 15:17.310
So that's it...

15:17.550 --> 15:21.940
The final push she needed was 
knowing that her own children

15:21.940 --> 15:24.940
were all plotting to kill her.

15:25.210 --> 15:29.310
Not only did she think she was going to 
bring about the downfall of the group,

15:29.310 --> 15:32.880
she also realized that all she'd done 
for the sake of her children's happiness

15:32.880 --> 15:35.190
had only made their lives worse.

15:35.190 --> 15:37.530
Suicide might've seemed like the only choice.

15:38.140 --> 15:42.620
After all, all her children wanted her dead.

15:42.620 --> 15:45.590
If Grandfather deliberately showed her this,

15:45.590 --> 15:49.580
then perhaps we can say that 
he's the one who killed her.

15:50.250 --> 15:52.090
And in a sense, my brother,

15:52.340 --> 15:57.340
Kaoruko, Koya-san, and I all 
had a hand in her death.

15:59.470 --> 16:00.520
I'm not sure.

16:00.520 --> 16:03.850
It's hard to say if even the president 
would've been able to figure it out.

16:04.130 --> 16:05.260
At the time,

16:05.260 --> 16:09.400
I'm sure you were all pursuing your 
murder plots carefully, and in secret.

16:09.400 --> 16:12.100
Perhaps he'd simply created false evidence

16:12.100 --> 16:15.580
that made it look like you 
were plotting to kill her,

16:15.580 --> 16:18.280
in order to drive her to suicide.

16:18.570 --> 16:23.320
It's more natural to assume that he lied, 
and by chance, his lies came true.

16:23.320 --> 16:25.530
That's very kind of you to say.

16:25.530 --> 16:27.630
But this is still partially 
our responsibility.

16:27.630 --> 16:30.510
We shouldn't make Dad take all the blame.

16:30.810 --> 16:32.900
Like Iwanaga-san said,

16:32.900 --> 16:37.220
if Grandfather had just told you this, 
you wouldn't have accepted it.

16:37.550 --> 16:39.740
Unless you first assumed he was the killer,

16:39.740 --> 16:43.310
then found out that you were 
all plotting her murder,

16:43.540 --> 16:47.300
and then finally objectively looked at 
the position she was in at the time,

16:47.300 --> 16:49.460
you wouldn't have believed it.

16:50.220 --> 16:55.700
You were asked by my grandfather to 
lead us to this truth, weren't you?

16:55.700 --> 16:59.620
President Otonashi never 
felt that was necessary.

17:00.040 --> 17:03.860
Now, do you two agree with Rion-san's answer?

17:04.170 --> 17:06.250
If so, I'll consider this your final answer,

17:06.250 --> 17:10.500
and present it to President 
Otonashi tomorrow at noon.

17:10.970 --> 17:13.420
There's no better answer to be had.

17:13.420 --> 17:14.760
I agree.

17:14.990 --> 17:18.260
What will you do with the rights 
to the inheritance, then?

17:18.760 --> 17:21.510
It was Rion-san who came up with this answer.

17:21.510 --> 17:24.310
Will you still follow the rules 
you laid out at the start?

17:24.560 --> 17:26.990
After trying to kill my mother,

17:26.990 --> 17:30.650
how am I supposed to ask for 
priority rights to her inheritance?

17:30.650 --> 17:32.610
I'm sure Kaoruko feels the same.

17:32.610 --> 17:36.150
If she was the kind of person who 
could ask for priority after this,

17:36.150 --> 17:39.060
she wouldn't have been afraid of 
the question in the first place.

17:39.700 --> 17:42.280
Does anybody really need 
priority at this point?

17:42.280 --> 17:45.350
Just have Grandfather split it up.

17:45.830 --> 17:48.120
Let's tell the president that, then.

17:49.190 --> 17:54.420
Rion-san, can you give your answer 
to the president directly tomorrow?

17:54.740 --> 17:57.340
I can, if you'd rather not.

17:57.560 --> 17:59.820
I'll do it myself.

17:59.820 --> 18:03.550
If I let you do it, you'll probably make 
them all seem worse than they are.

18:03.950 --> 18:06.310
The name "Rion" has a nice ring to it.

18:06.310 --> 18:08.910
It's like a combination of 
"squirrel (risu)" and "lion."

18:08.910 --> 18:11.990
Cute and brave. Just like you.

18:13.770 --> 18:16.410
Where did that come from?

18:16.410 --> 18:19.930
It's just the English spelling 
of "lion" put into Japanese.

18:20.580 --> 18:23.780
My brother always did love lions.

18:23.780 --> 18:27.000
If you were a boy, 
he might've called you Reo.

18:27.380 --> 18:30.380
You know him so well.

18:30.380 --> 18:33.410
Why don't you take this as an 
opportunity to make amends?

18:34.900 --> 18:36.600
I'll think about it.

18:37.420 --> 18:40.310
But first, I need to visit Mom's grave.

18:40.310 --> 18:44.010
In her own way, she was trying to protect 
things that needed to be protected.

18:44.010 --> 18:47.140
I need to pay my respects.

18:47.140 --> 18:50.830
And I need to tell Kaoruko, too, I guess.

18:51.730 --> 18:56.100
But would it be better to wait until we 
get certainty from the president tomorrow?

19:01.410 --> 19:03.910
<b>September 4th</b>

19:01.860 --> 19:06.410
This is our answer. 
What do you think, Grandfather?

19:12.330 --> 19:15.800
I should've done this sooner.

19:15.800 --> 19:19.040
Ryoma, Susumu, Kaoruko, Koya-kun,

19:19.040 --> 19:23.430
I've made you all suffer from 
more guilt than you deserved.

19:27.410 --> 19:29.450
Your answer is correct.

19:29.930 --> 19:35.820
But I didn't know you were all 
planning to kill your mother.

19:35.820 --> 19:37.570
That was pure coincidence.

19:40.580 --> 19:47.070
I am glad, though, that I put my own plan 
to kill her into effect before you did.

19:47.070 --> 19:52.260
I was able to avoid making 
you kill your own mother.

19:52.260 --> 19:58.670
No, it's still true that 
all of us have sinned.

19:58.890 --> 20:01.500
It's not a crime that can be judged 
in a court of law, though.

20:01.500 --> 20:06.270
And I've got no proof, but I don't 
think Mom would hate you.

20:06.270 --> 20:09.530
Back then, we all were doing 
the only things we could do.

20:10.100 --> 20:13.230
Everyone has times when they 
want to kill someone else.

20:13.230 --> 20:15.980
Or even times when they'll pick up a 
deadly weapon and try to kill them.

20:15.980 --> 20:20.570
But whether or not you cross that 
last line makes a big difference.

20:20.570 --> 20:23.540
I will take the responsibility 
for killing Sumi-san.

20:23.540 --> 20:27.330
All you need to do is watch me die.

20:29.370 --> 20:30.950
I've kept this from you,

20:30.950 --> 20:34.330
but I've been suffering from 
malignant tumors for a long time.

20:35.470 --> 20:37.920
The doctors say that in six months, 
I won't be able to walk.

20:37.920 --> 20:42.790
I'll be in constant pain and eventually
die an awful, miserable death.

20:43.300 --> 20:47.820
This illness and pain are the 
price I pay for killing Sumi-san.

20:50.310 --> 20:53.730
I will not choose death with dignity 
or take any drugs to ease the pain.

20:53.730 --> 20:56.380
I shall accept my suffering until 
the last moment of my life.

20:56.940 --> 21:00.220
Murder carries a steep price.

21:00.220 --> 21:04.760
A price that must be paid 
even if you don't get caught.

21:04.760 --> 21:09.210
You must never think it normal to 
succeed after committing such a sin.

21:09.620 --> 21:13.450
They've all decided not to ask 
for priority in the inheritance.

21:13.680 --> 21:16.620
Rion-san did the most to 
come up with the answer,

21:16.880 --> 21:20.360
but she says you can divide 
the inheritance as you like.

21:22.630 --> 21:24.760
Most people would be more greedy.

21:24.760 --> 21:27.400
No, I think it's the natural decision.

21:28.330 --> 21:31.960
You've done more than anyone, Kotoko-san.

21:31.960 --> 21:35.500
I'm glad I asked you to do this. 
You have my thanks.

21:40.440 --> 21:43.180
I think it's too soon for you to thank me.

21:46.180 --> 21:52.630
If you'd killed her with your own hands, 
I wouldn't have needed to say anything.

21:53.370 --> 21:56.750
But you picked a method that's 
much more your style.

21:57.160 --> 22:01.000
You should be a little more aware 
that what you did was wrong.

22:01.280 --> 22:05.600
Right now, you're thinking that 
the method you chose was right.

22:05.600 --> 22:10.760
As you said, you were able to keep your 
children from killing their mother.

22:11.220 --> 22:16.640
But that means you don't regret the 
choice you made, or your success.

22:17.770 --> 22:18.760
Rion-san.

22:19.270 --> 22:22.520
Your claim was that Otonashi 
Sumi-san killed herself.

22:22.520 --> 22:27.150
But why not make it look like an accident?

22:27.150 --> 22:28.610
Because...

22:28.610 --> 22:31.990
She could have dropped something and 
run out into the road to pick it up,

22:32.210 --> 22:36.560
or slipped and fallen off a train platform.

22:36.560 --> 22:40.260
There were any number of options, 
if she wanted to take them.

22:40.260 --> 22:45.170
On the surface, she didn't look 
like someone who'd commit suicide.

22:45.170 --> 22:48.420
Even if her death was slightly unnatural, 
it still would have been ruled an accident.

22:48.420 --> 22:50.050
K-Kotoko-san...

22:50.050 --> 22:53.430
Then there would've been 
no police investigation.

22:53.720 --> 22:56.310
No need to look into alibis.

22:56.690 --> 23:00.230
In fact, Kaoruko-san's 
alibi almost fell apart.

23:00.230 --> 23:03.520
Without that broken bone, 
she wouldn't have had one.

23:03.520 --> 23:06.700
And if the police had done a 
more thorough investigation,

23:06.700 --> 23:09.250
they might have seen through her 
efforts to make it look like suicide.

23:09.610 --> 23:12.200
Making it look like murder was a risky move.

23:12.520 --> 23:15.830
Which means that she didn't do it.

23:16.620 --> 23:21.500
Otonashi Sumi-san's death was 
no suicide. It was murder.

23:21.500 --> 23:24.860
Now, let me tell you who the real killer is.

23:27.000 --> 23:30.030
To be continued
